From fb821048b9ce669bad27362ebce543d8e29cab5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:12:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/44] arm64: dts: apple: t6020-j414s: add an opt-in PMP
 variant

The J414s DT is built without APPLE_USE_PMP, so the PMP coprocessor is
never booted: the pmp node stays disabled, m1n1 finds no pmp alias to fill
in, and the DCP, dcpext, AVD and ISP power domains bypass their PMP report
entries. Asahi measured about 0.5 W idle saving from booting the PMP on a
14" M1 Pro; the T602x nodes and report offsets already exist.

t6020-j414s-pmp.dts defines APPLE_USE_PMP and includes the board. It is
not in the Makefile: it has the J414s compatible and m1n1 boots the last
matching DTB, so packaging it would turn the PMP on for every J414s.
Build it by name and bundle it into m1n1's stage 2 to test it.

test_t6020_pmp.py compiles both boards and checks that the sources differ
only by the pmp alias and the five power-domains lines, that the PMP node
stays disabled until m1n1 fills it in, and that the Makefile does not list
the variant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
